WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.195
"What do you mean?" Zann asked Gliss. "What did you find out while you were a prisoner?"

2
00:00:10.196 --> 00:00:12.830
"Is it something about Morb?" Darb asked.

3
00:00:12.831 --> 00:00:18.301
Gliss' lower lip trembled. "Yes," she said. "And it's horrible!"

4
00:00:18.302 --> 00:00:20.862
"Tell us," Perda urged.

5
00:00:20.863 --> 00:00:26.396
"A few of the other Reds understood the trolls' language," Gliss said.

6
00:00:26.397 --> 00:00:29.698
"They listened when our guards talked to one another.

7
00:00:29.699 --> 00:00:36.375
The trolls kept grumbling about having to keep us at the zoo instead of zapping us back to Morb's fortress."

8
00:00:36.376 --> 00:00:39.338
"We were wondering about that too," Darb said.

9
00:00:39.339 --> 00:00:46.417
Zann nodded. "We guessed it might be because Morb used up all his power kidnapping the king and queen."

10
00:00:46.418 --> 00:00:53.131
"That's not why," Gliss said. "Kidnapping the king and queen gave Morb even more power.

11
00:00:53.132 --> 00:01:00.374
He left the trolls alone because he's busy building a horrible machine to steal all of the magical energy in Magica!"

12
00:01:00.375 --> 00:01:04.342
Perda gasped. "What? That's impossible!"

13
00:01:04.343 --> 00:01:07.538
"That's what I thought at first," Gliss said.

14
00:01:07.539 --> 00:01:12.771
"I figured the trolls must be confused. Everyone knows they're pretty dumb.

15
00:01:12.772 --> 00:01:15.898
But then I talked to a woman named Saffa."

16
00:01:15.899 --> 00:01:21.988
"She's one of Boz's Magic Master friends," Zann said. "What did she say?"

17
00:01:21.989 --> 00:01:26.983
"Saffa knows about an ancient text from the Old Times," Gliss replied.

18
00:01:26.984 --> 00:01:30.978
"It contains plans for building a machine that could do what the trolls said—suck

19
00:01:30.979 --> 00:01:38.021
the power out of Reds, regular people, dragons, message moths, mood trees, whatever. Anything

20
00:01:38.022 --> 00:01:41.825
or anyone with any magic at all." Zann

21
00:01:41.826 --> 00:01:49.882
gulped. "So if Morb succeeded in building this machine, he would control all the magic in Magica?" Gliss

22
00:01:49.883 --> 00:01:54.756
nodded. "Saffa said the Old Times ended because of that machine. An

23
00:01:54.757 --> 00:02:02.544
extremely powerful and evil magician invented it, and when people realized what the machine could do, they were shocked. People

24
00:02:02.545 --> 00:02:11.135
decided no one person should have that much power, and that Magica needed laws to protect the weak from the strong." "That

25
00:02:11.136 --> 00:02:15.173
was when the first Red Council was formed," Darb put in. "The

26
00:02:15.174 --> 00:02:18.701
first thing the members did was enact the Days of Discipline. I've

27
00:02:18.702 --> 00:02:23.261
read a lot about that—but I've never heard of the magic-sucking machine." "How

28
00:02:23.262 --> 00:02:27.833
could Morb get his hands on those plans?" Zann wondered. "Teplo

29
00:02:27.834 --> 00:02:32.501
says all the ancient texts are locked away at the university." "Saffa

30
00:02:32.502 --> 00:02:39.770
suspects there's another copy of the text hidden deep within the Cave of the Unknown," Gliss said. "How

31
00:02:39.771 --> 00:02:42.976
would Morb have found it?" Perda asked. "Even

32
00:02:42.977 --> 00:02:47.916
the most powerful Magic Masters don't dare go too deep in there." Gliss

33
00:02:47.917 --> 00:02:51.995
shrugged. "Who knows? But if he did . . ." Her

34
00:02:51.996 --> 00:02:53.848
voice trailed off. For

35
00:02:53.849 --> 00:02:57.221
a moment the kids all stared at one another in silence. Zann

36
00:02:57.222 --> 00:03:00.878
was the first to speak. "We have to warn somebody. If

37
00:03:00.879 --> 00:03:06.077
this is true, Morb needs to be stopped before it's too late." "Let's

38
00:03:06.078 --> 00:03:08.619
go to the palace," Perda said. "Yog

39
00:03:08.620 --> 00:03:11.662
will be able to get word to Venna from there."

40
00:03:11.663 --> 00:03:16.380
"Wait!" Gliss broke in. "Let's just wait for Fala to get back.

41
00:03:16.381 --> 00:03:19.933
She's not a Red—it's safer for her to go."

42
00:03:19.934 --> 00:03:26.692
"But if Morb really is working on this magic-sucking machine, there's no time to waste!" Perda said.

43
00:03:26.693 --> 00:03:33.829
Zann knew that Perda was right. But he still felt guilty about convincing Gliss to zap out of the palace earlier.

44
00:03:33.830 --> 00:03:37.576
He didn't want to talk her into something else that could be dangerous.

45
00:03:37.577 --> 00:03:41.480
"Why don't you stay here while the rest of us go?" he suggested.

46
00:03:41.481 --> 00:03:43.851
"You can tell Fala where we went."

47
00:03:43.852 --> 00:03:48.336
"No!" Gliss said. "If you're all going, I'm going too."

48
00:03:48.337 --> 00:03:55.824
"Okay," Zann agreed. Obviously Gliss didn't want to be alone.

49
00:03:55.825 --> 00:03:59.239
It didn't take long for Zann and his friends to reach the palace.

50
00:03:59.240 --> 00:04:03.845
A stout man with a bristly brown beard was standing guard at the main entrance.

51
00:04:03.846 --> 00:04:10.439
"No visitors," he said without even looking at the kids. "Official business only today."

52
00:04:10.440 --> 00:04:14.293
"We are here on official business," Perda said.

53
00:04:14.294 --> 00:04:17.466
"We need to talk to Yog. Or Rixa."

54
00:04:17.467 --> 00:04:22.798
The guard glanced at her, looking skeptical. "What's your business?"

55
00:04:22.799 --> 00:04:27.905
"Please, just tell Yog or Rixa that we're here," Zann said.

56
00:04:27.906 --> 00:04:31.817
The guard's jaw dropped as he noticed Zann's hair color.

57
00:04:31.818 --> 00:04:37.129
"Reds!" he exclaimed. "What did you say your names were again?"

58
00:04:37.130 --> 00:04:41.317
Zann and his friends waited impatiently while the guard sent a message moth.

59
00:04:41.318 --> 00:04:44.318
Soon the moth returned with a new message.

60
00:04:44.319 --> 00:04:48.226
The guard read it. "Rixa says to let you in.

61
00:04:48.227 --> 00:04:51.650
You'll find her in the throne room with Slib."

62
00:04:51.651 --> 00:04:55.111
Zann wondered if that meant Slib had taken over the government.

63
00:04:55.112 --> 00:05:04.587
"Thanks," he said. He and his friends hurried inside before the guard could change his mind about letting them in.

64
00:05:04.588 --> 00:05:09.510
Then they stopped. "Do you remember how to get to the throne room?" Gliss asked.

65
00:05:09.511 --> 00:05:13.556
"How could I? We crawled in through a tunnel and zapped out."

66
00:05:13.557 --> 00:05:17.984
Perda glanced up and down the hallway. "Wait, is that it?"

67
00:05:17.985 --> 00:05:22.623
The kids could see a large, arched doorway farther down the hall, and they hurried to it.

68
00:05:22.624 --> 00:05:26.005
Zann peered in and saw a large crowd of adults.

69
00:05:26.006 --> 00:05:29.316
"Do you see Rixa or Yog?" Gliss whispered.

70
00:05:29.317 --> 00:05:33.888
Zann couldn't see Yog anywhere. But he spotted Rixa arguing with Slib.

71
00:05:33.889 --> 00:05:38.080
Before he could point her out, a burst of magical energy filled the room.

72
00:05:38.081 --> 00:05:45.059
Morb appeared in front of the thrones—along with half a dozen trolls and a cloud of tiny, buzzing dragons.

73
00:05:45.060 --> 00:05:48.320
Thinking fast, Zann pulled his friends out of sight.

74
00:05:48.321 --> 00:05:52.863
His heart pounded with fear. Had Morb tracked them here somehow?

75
00:05:52.864 --> 00:05:55.405
Morb didn't even glance in their direction though.

76
00:05:55.406 --> 00:05:58.474
He stared at the stunned adults with a smile.

77
00:05:58.475 --> 00:06:04.287
"Hello again," he said. "I liked it here so much that I decided to return."

78
00:06:04.288 --> 00:06:07.500
He stepped over to the king's throne and sat down.

79
00:06:07.501 --> 00:06:14.413
"And this time I think I'll stay."

